WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:32.095
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:32.365 --> 00:39.372
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:42.333 --> 00:45.253
‎Please stop anyone ‎who approaches the stage.

4
00:45.336 --> 00:47.297
‎-I'll do that. ‎-Thank you.

5
00:53.344 --> 00:54.220
‎Pi-o.

6
00:55.430 --> 00:57.807
‎Just one more time. Please?

7
00:58.850 --> 01:00.310
‎Think this over one more time.

8
01:01.478 --> 01:02.812
‎Once you go in,

9
01:03.688 --> 01:05.023
‎there's no turning back.

10
01:06.524 --> 01:08.193
‎I gave this a lot of thought.

11
01:09.152 --> 01:09.986
‎Thank you.

12
01:42.936 --> 01:44.270
‎My mother isn't the only one

13
01:45.480 --> 01:47.565
‎to blame for the abduction.

14
01:49.234 --> 01:50.151
‎I'm the one who used

15
01:51.319 --> 01:53.446
‎Conductor Choi Jeong-yo's sheet music

16
01:53.530 --> 01:55.698
‎to win the competition.

17
01:57.242 --> 01:58.076
‎Therefore,

18
01:59.202 --> 02:02.372
‎this entire incident happened ‎because of my own greed.

19
02:02.455 --> 02:07.877
‎Once again, I sincerely apologize ‎to Conductor Choi Jeong-yo…

20
02:10.338 --> 02:12.173
‎for the harm my mother and I caused.

21
02:14.134 --> 02:15.510
‎Therefore, as of today,

22
02:17.262 --> 02:18.972
‎I'm walking away from everything…

23
02:21.141 --> 02:22.392
‎I've been given.

24
02:23.726 --> 02:26.354
‎To everyone who has supported me…

25
02:28.398 --> 02:29.357
‎once again,

26
02:30.942 --> 02:32.610
‎I deeply apologize.

27
02:46.499 --> 02:48.877
‎What did you mean by winning ‎with his sheet music?

28
02:49.502 --> 02:51.588
‎Did you mean ‎you stole first place from him?

29
02:52.130 --> 02:54.465
‎Were you aware of your mother's crime?

30
02:54.549 --> 02:56.551
‎How long had you known about this?

31
02:56.634 --> 02:59.596
‎-Please elaborate. ‎-Please provide more specifics.

32
03:38.384 --> 03:40.178
‎FINALE

33
04:05.370 --> 04:07.080
‎HANKOOK SYMPHONY ANNOUNCEMENT CHAT

34
04:07.163 --> 04:11.000
‎REHEARSAL HAS BEEN POSTPONED ‎DUE TO MAESTRO KANG'S EMERGENCY SURGERY.

35
04:16.631 --> 04:18.883
‎SURGERY STATUS ‎KANG SEUNG-****: IN PROGRESS

36
04:27.225 --> 04:29.227
‎How did the surgery go?

37
04:29.310 --> 04:31.020
‎We did everything we could,

38
04:31.521 --> 04:34.524
‎but his heart was ‎already severely weakened.

39
04:35.358 --> 04:38.027
‎I'm sorry, but you should ‎prepare for the worst.

40
04:40.154 --> 04:40.989
‎How?

41
04:42.407 --> 04:44.701
‎How could this happen?

42
05:00.133 --> 05:01.009
‎Mr. Kang.

43
05:02.302 --> 05:04.012
‎I'm right here.

44
05:05.221 --> 05:06.055
‎Mr. Kang?

45
05:09.434 --> 05:12.103
‎Can you hear me?

46
05:13.062 --> 05:13.980
‎Why…

47
05:15.857 --> 05:18.026
‎Why didn't you tell me?

48
05:19.027 --> 05:20.361
‎Why did you keep it from me

49
05:21.112 --> 05:24.073
‎until things got so out of hand?

50
05:30.538 --> 05:31.372
‎What?

51
05:33.958 --> 05:35.668
‎Pi-o…

52
05:43.634 --> 05:44.469
‎Pi-o.

53
05:46.429 --> 05:48.681
‎Mr. Kang just woke up from anesthesia.

54
05:49.515 --> 05:50.558
‎He's asking for you.

55
05:52.268 --> 05:55.146
‎But he wants to see ‎you and Jeong-yo together.

56
05:55.730 --> 05:57.273
‎I think it's best if you call him.

57
06:23.883 --> 06:24.717
‎Hello?

58
06:26.135 --> 06:27.053
‎Where are you?

59
06:29.430 --> 06:30.681
‎How's Mr. Kang?

60
06:30.765 --> 06:32.266
‎He's out of surgery…

61
06:34.602 --> 06:35.895
‎and woke up from anesthesia.

62
06:35.978 --> 06:37.563
‎Then he's okay, right?

63
06:38.064 --> 06:38.981
‎No.

64
06:39.774 --> 06:40.858
‎The doctor said…

65
06:43.236 --> 06:44.612
‎we should prepare for the worst.

66
06:46.906 --> 06:49.158
‎He wants to see you one last time.

67
06:50.827 --> 06:52.036
‎Can you come?

68
07:37.665 --> 07:38.499
‎Mr. Kang.

69
07:39.459 --> 07:40.668
‎Mr. Kang?

70
07:41.252 --> 07:42.420
‎They're here.

71
07:55.057 --> 07:56.559
‎Go on in, Jeong-yo.

72
07:59.812 --> 08:01.105
‎Grandfather.

73
08:12.074 --> 08:13.159
‎I'm sorry.

74
08:15.870 --> 08:16.787
‎It's my fault.

75
08:18.247 --> 08:19.248
‎No.

76
08:21.584 --> 08:23.085
‎It's not your fault.

77
08:24.545 --> 08:26.547
‎It's just my time to go.

78
08:28.883 --> 08:30.760
‎Why are you sorry for that?

79
08:35.640 --> 08:37.141
‎So the two of you…

80
08:39.435 --> 08:42.146
‎have finally completed ‎Nemesis‎.

81
08:42.230 --> 08:43.856
‎You did it.

82
08:46.984 --> 08:47.860
‎Pi-o.

83
08:52.281 --> 08:55.535
‎I thought you'd spend your whole life ‎chasing after Jeong-yo,

84
08:55.618 --> 08:57.787
‎only to torment yourself.

85
08:58.996 --> 09:01.207
‎That living in someone's shadow…

86
09:02.375 --> 09:05.127
‎would slowly eat you alive.

87
09:06.170 --> 09:07.046
‎But…

88
09:09.048 --> 09:10.383
‎Now I realize…

89
09:11.842 --> 09:13.261
‎that I was the one…

90
09:15.888 --> 09:16.889
‎who held you back.

91
09:18.474 --> 09:20.351
‎I let my pride get the better of me…

92
09:22.603 --> 09:25.690
‎and put you through hell

93
09:25.773 --> 09:27.358
‎when you were so young.

94
09:28.693 --> 09:30.278
‎Please forgive me.

95
09:48.421 --> 09:49.797
‎I'm sorry, Jeong-yo.

96
09:50.590 --> 09:53.551
‎I apologize on my daughter's behalf.

97
09:54.719 --> 09:56.554
‎The way she turned out…

98
10:00.182 --> 10:01.726
‎is all my fault.

99
10:03.311 --> 10:06.188
‎My cowardly actions caught up with me…

100
10:08.357 --> 10:10.526
‎and you had to suffer for it.

101
10:11.986 --> 10:13.029
‎I'm sorry.

102
10:15.781 --> 10:17.074
‎I'm sorry.

103
10:18.117 --> 10:19.201
‎All of this…

104
10:21.120 --> 10:22.246
‎is my fault.

105
10:24.373 --> 10:26.125
‎So will you please…

106
10:29.962 --> 10:31.922
‎forgive my foolish child?

107
11:08.626 --> 11:09.502
‎Pi-o.

108
11:13.130 --> 11:14.048
‎You must've resented

109
11:15.424 --> 11:17.218
‎your grandfather all this time.

110
11:21.180 --> 11:22.098
‎Still,

111
11:24.016 --> 11:26.352
‎I hope you won't ‎hold too much against him.

112
11:29.647 --> 11:31.190
‎One time…

113
11:32.983 --> 11:35.694
‎I asked your grandfather

114
11:36.362 --> 11:38.155
‎why he was so harsh to you.

115
11:40.032 --> 11:41.242
‎And he said

116
11:42.451 --> 11:43.411
‎it was because

117
11:44.620 --> 11:46.247
‎you take after him.

118
11:48.874 --> 11:50.918
‎That you push yourself to the limit…

119
11:52.962 --> 11:55.923
‎then choose to self-destruct ‎if it doesn't work out.

120
11:56.006 --> 11:58.801
‎He said you were just like him ‎in that regard.

121
12:00.761 --> 12:02.012
‎I think

122
12:03.055 --> 12:05.599
‎he may have felt tormented

123
12:06.559 --> 12:08.519
‎because your pain

124
12:09.186 --> 12:11.689
‎was just too clear to him.

125
12:17.027 --> 12:18.070
‎Excuse me, ma'am.

126
12:18.863 --> 12:20.865
‎We have a few things to go over.

127
12:39.091 --> 12:40.050
‎Well,

128
12:40.634 --> 12:41.927
‎today wasn't half bad.

129
12:43.471 --> 12:45.681
‎Invite me to your next performance.

130
12:52.521 --> 12:53.856
‎Grandfather.

131
12:56.275 --> 12:57.985
‎Break the mold, Pi-o.

132
12:58.652 --> 13:01.155
‎Stop relying on that chunk of metal,

133
13:01.238 --> 13:03.949
‎and find your own inner rhythm.

134
13:18.380 --> 13:19.715
‎Pi-o.

135
13:20.299 --> 13:22.384
‎Yes, Grandfather?

136
13:26.180 --> 13:30.643
‎I want to hear your rendition ‎of the ‎Moonlight Sonata.

137
13:58.045 --> 13:59.255
‎How nice.

138
14:00.673 --> 14:01.549
‎Grandfather.

139
14:02.716 --> 14:03.968
‎When you get better,

140
14:04.051 --> 14:06.804
‎I'll play you a version ‎that's even better than this.

141
14:07.972 --> 14:09.139
‎You see,

142
14:09.223 --> 14:11.725
‎I think I can play from the heart now.

143
14:18.941 --> 14:20.150
‎Let me be alone…

144
14:22.653 --> 14:25.239
‎with the music for a moment.

145
14:30.119 --> 14:31.036
‎Okay.

146
15:37.353 --> 15:38.562
‎Grandfather?

147
15:43.067 --> 15:44.068
‎Grandfather.

148
15:44.151 --> 15:45.277
‎Grandfather.

149
15:46.570 --> 15:48.113
‎Grandfather!

150
16:13.389 --> 16:15.599
‎In accordance with our custom,

151
16:15.683 --> 16:18.185
‎we now commit this body to the ground.

152
16:19.436 --> 16:24.984
‎Lord, grant eternal rest to our brother, ‎Kang Seung-woon John.

153
16:25.693 --> 16:29.196
‎-May perpetual light shine upon him. ‎-May perpetual light shine upon him.

154
16:29.947 --> 16:34.243
‎Receive his soul and present him

155
16:34.326 --> 16:35.619
‎to God the Most High.

156
16:36.161 --> 16:38.122
‎Most merciful Father,

157
16:38.205 --> 16:42.751
‎we are filled with the sure hope ‎that our departed will rise again…

158
16:48.340 --> 16:50.759
‎THE LATE KANG SEUNG-WOON JOHN ‎FUNERAL MASS

159
16:50.843 --> 16:52.553
‎Father…

160
16:54.555 --> 16:56.348
‎This is all your fault, Father.

161
16:57.516 --> 17:01.270
‎If you had been kind to Pi-o, ‎I wouldn't have done it.

162
17:02.730 --> 17:04.898
‎If only you had acknowledged him,

163
17:04.982 --> 17:07.234
‎I wouldn't have done something this crazy!

164
17:07.317 --> 17:08.694
‎How could you do that?

165
17:08.777 --> 17:10.195
‎How could you do that to me?

166
17:10.279 --> 17:11.488
‎How could you do that to Pi-o?

167
17:11.572 --> 17:12.906
‎Explain yourself!

168
17:12.990 --> 17:16.410
‎How could you do that?

169
17:20.164 --> 17:21.957
‎How could you?

170
17:22.041 --> 17:25.502
‎How could you do that, Father?

171
17:35.387 --> 17:37.264
‎OPENING THE FUTURE ‎THROUGH ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

172
17:37.347 --> 17:40.309
‎Ms. Kang has refused to receive visitors.

173
18:04.500 --> 18:08.545
‎KANG PI-O

174
18:49.169 --> 18:51.713
‎Do you really have to do this?

175
19:03.559 --> 19:04.476
‎I get it.

176
19:04.560 --> 19:06.603
‎I know you're heartbroken.

177
19:06.687 --> 19:09.231
‎-But saying you'll never play-- ‎-Please stop.

178
19:10.899 --> 19:12.484
‎I'll never play again.

179
19:14.528 --> 19:15.821
‎All of this happened

180
19:15.904 --> 19:18.407
‎because of my greed.

181
19:20.450 --> 19:21.493
‎His piano is up for sale.

182
19:21.577 --> 19:23.328
‎-Hello. ‎-Are you serious?

183
19:24.204 --> 19:26.623
‎Kang Pi-o's piano is up for sale?

184
19:26.707 --> 19:29.877
‎Yeah. Looks like he's really quitting.

185
19:29.960 --> 19:32.337
‎Jeez, that idiot.

186
19:32.421 --> 19:34.506
‎I thought he finally got his touch back.

187
19:34.590 --> 19:36.008
‎Then again,

188
19:36.091 --> 19:38.343
‎if he thinks Maestro Kang died ‎because of him,

189
19:38.427 --> 19:40.846
‎how could he bring himself to play again?

190
19:41.638 --> 19:42.848
‎I know, right?

191
19:43.390 --> 19:47.352
‎Who'd have known such a powerful family ‎would end up in ruins like this?

192
19:48.020 --> 19:49.980
‎Anyway, pianists everywhere

193
19:50.063 --> 19:53.066
‎are fighting over it, ‎even offering to pay a premium.

194
19:55.360 --> 19:56.820
‎Why is your phone turned off?

195
19:58.113 --> 19:59.031
‎Oh…

196
19:59.114 --> 20:00.407
‎You have a guest.

197
20:00.490 --> 20:02.326
‎He's been waiting all afternoon.

198
20:02.409 --> 20:05.954
‎I told him to return later, ‎but he insisted on waiting.

199
20:14.546 --> 20:15.589
‎What are you doing here?

200
20:16.215 --> 20:17.257
‎Take a seat.

201
20:26.183 --> 20:27.100
‎Why did you come?

202
20:27.184 --> 20:28.977
‎Why did you sell your piano?

203
20:30.520 --> 20:31.772
‎That's why you're here?

204
20:31.855 --> 20:32.814
‎Yeah.

205
20:35.275 --> 20:36.485
‎Because I don't need it anymore.

206
20:42.908 --> 20:46.078
‎I asked Mr. Kang something ‎before he passed away.

207
20:47.704 --> 20:50.874
‎I asked if he believed flawed artists ‎don't deserve to make art.

208
20:51.458 --> 20:52.834
‎Then he told me

209
20:53.710 --> 20:57.297
‎that if anything, ‎one must be flawed to make art.

210
21:00.634 --> 21:02.427
‎So keep playing the piano.

211
21:03.470 --> 21:04.930
‎All we can do is…

212
21:06.348 --> 21:08.183
‎just keep making music.

213
21:10.060 --> 21:11.520
‎Thanks for saying that.

214
21:12.104 --> 21:12.938
‎But…

215
21:14.022 --> 21:16.400
‎I can't forgive myself.

216
21:17.067 --> 21:19.278
‎It's because I insisted on pursuing music

217
21:19.361 --> 21:22.948
‎that my mom ended up the way she did ‎and my grandfather died.

218
21:25.993 --> 21:27.160
‎I'm responsible for your hand too.

219
21:59.151 --> 22:00.902
‎HYUN-CHUL

220
22:01.862 --> 22:02.779
‎Hello?

221
22:02.863 --> 22:04.156
‎The hospital called.

222
22:04.823 --> 22:06.158
‎He wants to see you.

223
22:08.035 --> 22:10.704
‎I guess he already knew you were back.

224
22:11.830 --> 22:12.998
‎He called a nurse over

225
22:13.081 --> 22:15.167
‎and told her he wanted to see you.

226
22:16.001 --> 22:19.629
‎I guess it'd be weird if he didn't know, ‎since you were all over the news.

227
22:23.967 --> 22:25.969
‎Our project is over now, right?

228
22:27.137 --> 22:28.388
‎Regardless of how it went down,

229
22:28.472 --> 22:30.348
‎they're paying for what they did.

230
22:32.142 --> 22:33.810
‎But why don't I feel relieved?

231
22:37.606 --> 22:39.024
‎You wanted to see me?

232
22:40.984 --> 22:42.778
‎When did you find out I returned?

233
22:43.779 --> 22:47.240
‎When you first got back to Korea.

234
22:47.824 --> 22:50.202
‎Then why are you only reaching out now?

235
22:53.997 --> 22:55.415
‎I felt like I had no right to.

236
23:01.546 --> 23:02.964
‎Here, have some.

237
23:03.048 --> 23:04.508
‎I know you like it.

238
23:05.842 --> 23:06.676
‎Why did you do it?

239
23:08.220 --> 23:10.847
‎You should've just let me die in a ditch.

240
23:12.808 --> 23:14.559
‎Why did you waste your money on me?

241
23:17.062 --> 23:19.523
‎Because you were good to me, ‎if only briefly.

242
23:21.233 --> 23:22.984
‎I know you want to forget,

243
23:23.735 --> 23:25.904
‎but you were good to me when I was young.

244
23:27.989 --> 23:29.574
‎And I wanted to repay you for that.

245
23:30.700 --> 23:31.535
‎Back then,

246
23:33.078 --> 23:34.287
‎I took my anger out on you.

247
23:35.497 --> 23:36.790
‎I'm sorry I did that.

248
23:38.041 --> 23:39.000
‎From now on…

249
23:40.627 --> 23:42.170
‎don't spend your money on me.

250
23:42.254 --> 23:44.172
‎I've got blood on my hands.

251
23:49.261 --> 23:50.637
‎I killed your mom.

252
23:52.347 --> 23:54.599
‎I raged about how she betrayed me,

253
23:55.600 --> 23:56.935
‎yet I refused to divorce her.

254
23:57.894 --> 24:00.313
‎I kept her close and tormented her

255
24:01.273 --> 24:02.816
‎until her last breath.

256
24:03.316 --> 24:04.317
‎In the end…

257
24:06.903 --> 24:09.114
‎I drained the life out of your mother.

258
24:10.532 --> 24:12.325
‎I expected to feel relief.

259
24:12.909 --> 24:15.912
‎But instead, it turns out…

260
24:17.914 --> 24:19.541
‎I just destroyed myself.

261
24:33.221 --> 24:34.806
‎I expected to feel relief.

262
24:35.515 --> 24:38.226
‎But instead, it turns out…

263
24:39.269 --> 24:40.896
‎I just destroyed myself.

264
24:43.899 --> 24:45.734
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

265
24:54.701 --> 24:55.660
‎What is it?

266
24:55.744 --> 24:56.786
‎What are you doing?

267
24:56.870 --> 24:58.246
‎Why are you calling?

268
24:58.830 --> 25:00.874
‎Come outside. I'm at your house.

269
25:12.427 --> 25:13.428
‎Why are you here again?

270
25:13.511 --> 25:16.306
‎Come with me. ‎I want to show you something.

271
25:31.947 --> 25:33.573
‎Why are we taking the bus?

272
25:34.824 --> 25:36.117
‎Just because.

273
25:36.201 --> 25:37.619
‎Brings back memories, right?

274
25:47.087 --> 25:47.921
‎Why are we here?

275
26:09.109 --> 26:10.110
‎What's this?

276
26:10.735 --> 26:13.113
‎What do you think? It's your piano.

277
26:13.697 --> 26:14.990
‎I bought it back.

278
26:15.073 --> 26:16.116
‎Yes, but why?

279
26:16.199 --> 26:18.702
‎Because you'll need it ‎when you play again.

280
26:19.703 --> 26:20.829
‎I said I'm done.

281
26:20.912 --> 26:22.831
‎You shouldn't have wasted your time.

282
26:29.379 --> 26:30.839
‎Sit down.

283
27:23.391 --> 27:24.517
‎What's going on?

284
27:25.101 --> 27:27.103
‎Why? You surprised?

285
27:27.812 --> 27:31.066
‎I kept up with my hospital treatments ‎just in case.

286
27:31.149 --> 27:34.110
‎Then somehow, my fingers started working.

287
27:35.987 --> 27:36.988
‎Well?

288
27:37.072 --> 27:38.365
‎Was it any good?

289
27:44.662 --> 27:45.914
‎Does this mean…

290
27:47.624 --> 27:49.209
‎you can play the piano again?

291
27:50.752 --> 27:51.586
‎Yeah.

292
27:55.256 --> 27:57.258
‎What's that look for?

293
27:59.344 --> 28:02.305
‎Now do you understand ‎why I dragged you all the way here?

294
28:03.932 --> 28:04.891
‎At the very least,

295
28:05.475 --> 28:08.144
‎I want you to stop ‎feeling guilty about me.

296
28:10.355 --> 28:11.856
‎And do me one last favor.

297
28:16.277 --> 28:17.445
‎Play the piano again.

298
28:22.283 --> 28:23.243
‎I thought about

299
28:24.244 --> 28:27.664
‎why I started playing the piano again ‎when I was young.

300
28:29.040 --> 28:31.501
‎You just came out of nowhere

301
28:31.584 --> 28:33.086
‎and stormed into my miserable life.

302
28:34.254 --> 28:35.713
‎You think playing the piano is a joke?

303
28:36.214 --> 28:40.427
‎You made me ashamed ‎of how I refused to take music seriously.

304
28:40.510 --> 28:42.303
‎We practiced this hundreds of times.

305
28:42.387 --> 28:44.514
‎Ignore everyone else.

306
28:44.597 --> 28:46.307
‎Forget where we are.

307
28:46.391 --> 28:49.018
‎I was drowning in my trauma,

308
28:49.102 --> 28:50.770
‎but you pulled me out.

309
28:51.396 --> 28:52.230
‎Play freely…

310
28:53.690 --> 28:54.774
‎like that day.

311
28:55.525 --> 28:57.026
‎Looking back,

312
28:58.486 --> 29:00.405
‎when I was lost in despair,

313
29:00.488 --> 29:03.283
‎you were the one ‎who pulled me back into music.

314
29:03.366 --> 29:05.535
‎Whether you meant to be or not,

315
29:06.411 --> 29:09.122
‎you were my light and hope.

316
29:11.207 --> 29:13.793
‎Even when I was consumed by revenge…

317
29:16.171 --> 29:19.632
‎I'd fall asleep dreaming of ‎playing four hands with you.

318
29:22.635 --> 29:24.846
‎Then I heard you were quitting the piano,

319
29:24.929 --> 29:26.139
‎so how do you think I felt?

320
29:27.682 --> 29:28.933
‎But…

321
29:30.101 --> 29:31.770
‎I stole your sheet music.

322
29:34.481 --> 29:36.232
‎And I stole your life.

323
29:36.316 --> 29:38.485
‎Man, you're so frustrating.

324
29:39.569 --> 29:40.904
‎Hey, Kang Pi-o.

325
29:42.405 --> 29:45.492
‎You interpreted that piece ‎and made it complete.

326
29:45.575 --> 29:46.785
‎The place you're at…

327
29:48.536 --> 29:50.163
‎was always yours.

328
29:51.998 --> 29:53.166
‎Neither of us can survive…

329
29:56.419 --> 29:59.255
‎unless we're immersed in music.

330
29:59.964 --> 30:03.343
‎We were born that way. Don't you get it?

331
30:07.597 --> 30:09.599
‎Remember Bach's Cantata No. 106?

332
30:14.145 --> 30:15.063
‎Get over here.

333
30:30.995 --> 30:31.996
‎All right.

334
30:32.622 --> 30:33.873
‎I'll play secondo.

335
30:34.707 --> 30:35.667
‎You play primo.

336
30:37.210 --> 30:38.253
‎Play freely…

337
30:39.796 --> 30:41.047
‎like that day.

338
32:28.071 --> 32:29.238
‎Thanks, Jeong-yo.

339
32:30.823 --> 32:31.908
‎You did it again.

340
32:33.785 --> 32:35.411
‎You pulled me out of my despair.

341
32:37.830 --> 32:38.873
‎No, I didn't.

342
32:40.291 --> 32:41.417
‎Didn't you hear what I said?

343
32:44.504 --> 32:46.172
‎It's really weird.

344
32:47.173 --> 32:48.466
‎We were at each other's throats,

345
32:48.549 --> 32:50.760
‎but whenever I was actually lost in music,

346
32:52.136 --> 32:53.346
‎you were always there.

347
32:54.806 --> 32:56.557
‎Ten years ago,

348
32:57.308 --> 32:59.268
‎when I said ‎I wouldn't enter any competitions

349
33:00.770 --> 33:04.107
‎and just wanted to be happy ‎making music with you…

350
33:06.651 --> 33:08.653
‎Looking back, that was the right call.

351
33:12.323 --> 33:13.449
‎It's not too late.

352
33:14.617 --> 33:16.119
‎Let's have fun making music.

353
33:20.373 --> 33:21.332
‎No way.

354
33:22.417 --> 33:26.212
‎I don't want to put up with ‎your same old prickly attitude.

355
33:27.463 --> 33:29.090
‎And the way I see it,

356
33:29.674 --> 33:31.801
‎you don't need my help anymore.

357
33:31.884 --> 33:34.429
‎Hey, just say no if you don't want to.

358
33:35.013 --> 33:36.431
‎You don't let things go, do you?

359
33:36.514 --> 33:37.640
‎Of course not.

360
33:38.516 --> 33:40.393
‎That's why I came after you.

361
33:45.314 --> 33:46.399
‎I had fun today.

362
33:48.067 --> 33:49.027
‎Thanks.

363
33:53.406 --> 33:55.199
‎Have a good night and rest well.

364
33:57.118 --> 33:58.369
‎See you around.

365
33:58.953 --> 33:59.871
‎Okay.

366
34:30.943 --> 34:31.819
‎Hello?

367
34:31.903 --> 34:33.196
‎Pi-o.

368
34:33.279 --> 34:35.740
‎Have you spoken to Jeong-yo recently?

369
34:36.574 --> 34:37.867
‎I saw him yesterday.

370
34:38.618 --> 34:39.786
‎Why?

371
34:39.869 --> 34:43.498
‎Jeong-yo put in his resignation ‎and won't answer his phone.

372
34:44.499 --> 34:46.542
‎Did he say anything yesterday?

373
34:51.464 --> 34:53.216
‎The phone is turned off.

374
34:53.299 --> 34:55.843
‎You will be connected to voicemail ‎after the beep‎…

375
34:57.804 --> 34:59.514
‎I think he prepared ahead of time.

376
35:00.223 --> 35:03.851
‎He emailed not just me ‎but the admin office and staff too.

377
35:04.352 --> 35:06.771
‎Are you sure he didn't mention anything?

378
35:09.148 --> 35:10.608
‎The phone is turned off.

379
35:10.691 --> 35:14.862
‎You will be connected to voicemail ‎after the beep…

380
35:40.471 --> 35:41.347
‎Kang Pi-o.

381
35:42.056 --> 35:43.558
‎I knew you'd come.

382
35:44.433 --> 35:46.394
‎By the time you find this letter,

383
35:47.019 --> 35:48.604
‎I'll be gone.

384
35:49.856 --> 35:50.815
‎I'm sorry,

385
35:51.691 --> 35:54.443
‎but I can't do that last favor for you.

386
35:57.488 --> 35:59.574
‎Maybe what happened between us…

387
36:01.909 --> 36:06.664
‎came from our deep longing ‎and love for music.

388
36:09.792 --> 36:12.253
‎Even though it caused a lot of pain,

389
36:12.336 --> 36:16.215
‎seeing your passion for music ‎taught me a great deal.

390
36:18.050 --> 36:19.135
‎So now,

391
36:19.927 --> 36:21.971
‎I'm leaving to make music ‎that comforts others

392
36:23.181 --> 36:26.517
‎rather than music ‎filled with resentment and hate.

393
36:27.393 --> 36:30.479
‎My misunderstandings caused you pain,

394
36:31.063 --> 36:33.774
‎but maybe I was obsessed ‎with getting revenge

395
36:35.151 --> 36:39.155
‎simply because I missed the days ‎we used to play piano together.

396
36:39.238 --> 36:42.158
‎MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE ‎TRADITIONAL MARKET

397
36:42.241 --> 36:43.492
‎I'm sorry for everything.

398
36:44.535 --> 36:45.494
‎And thank you.

399
36:46.871 --> 36:48.623
‎Whatever you do, don't give up.

400
36:48.706 --> 36:51.042
‎I hope you become a great musician.

401
37:14.815 --> 37:18.110
‎3 YEARS LATER

402
37:31.749 --> 37:32.750
‎Hey, Pi-o.

403
37:34.460 --> 37:36.212
‎Goodness, that looks amazing.

404
37:37.922 --> 37:40.216
‎You didn't have to come all this way ‎with your busy schedule.

405
37:40.299 --> 37:42.927
‎I kept saying I'd come, but I never did.

406
37:43.010 --> 37:45.388
‎So I was determined to come today.

407
37:47.056 --> 37:48.140
‎How's it coming along?

408
39:06.135 --> 39:07.970
‎How's running the agency? ‎Are you holding up?

409
39:08.763 --> 39:10.681
‎It's hard but fun.

410
39:10.765 --> 39:12.558
‎Now that I'm doing it myself,

411
39:12.641 --> 39:15.436
‎I totally understand ‎how hard it was for my mom.

412
39:16.228 --> 39:19.148
‎I have a whole new level ‎of respect for her now.

413
39:19.231 --> 39:21.108
‎Hyun-jeong is something else.

414
39:21.192 --> 39:23.819
‎How did she hand you the reins ‎and just walk away?

415
39:23.903 --> 39:25.154
‎Does she nag you?

416
39:25.905 --> 39:27.156
‎Not at all.

417
39:27.239 --> 39:30.451
‎But that stresses me out more, you know?

418
39:30.534 --> 39:32.078
‎I don't want to disappoint her.

419
39:33.579 --> 39:36.207
‎Jae-in, you're really becoming a grown-up.

420
39:37.875 --> 39:39.502
‎This is on the house.

421
39:41.003 --> 39:43.339
‎Just a little thank-you for the concert.

422
39:44.715 --> 39:45.800
‎Thank you.

423
39:46.425 --> 39:48.928
‎Call me anytime, and I'll come play.

424
39:49.011 --> 39:50.554
‎Really?

425
39:51.138 --> 39:53.557
‎Goodness, thank you. How wonderful.

426
39:53.641 --> 39:55.267
‎Please enjoy your meal.

427
39:55.851 --> 39:57.478
‎-Thank you. ‎-Thank you.

428
39:57.978 --> 40:00.773
‎As always, everyone loves you ‎wherever you go.

429
40:02.316 --> 40:04.652
‎-Go ask him. ‎-No, you do it.

430
40:05.236 --> 40:06.779
‎-Go ask. ‎-Hurry up and ask.

431
40:06.862 --> 40:08.823
‎-No, you ask him. ‎-No, you.

432
40:08.906 --> 40:10.199
‎Do you have something to ask?

433
40:11.992 --> 40:14.787
‎We watched your performance earlier.

434
40:15.454 --> 40:17.206
‎What's your name?

435
40:17.289 --> 40:19.250
‎You're famous, right? ‎Can we get an autograph?

436
40:21.627 --> 40:23.504
‎I'm not that famous.

437
40:30.010 --> 40:33.013
‎Still, I really liked your performance.

438
40:33.097 --> 40:34.098
‎Me too.

439
40:34.682 --> 40:35.599
‎Thanks.

440
40:36.225 --> 40:37.101
‎Enjoy your meal.

441
40:37.184 --> 40:38.185
‎-Thank you! ‎-Thank you!

442
40:38.978 --> 40:40.438
‎See? He's not famous.

443
40:40.521 --> 40:41.897
‎But my mom said that he is.

444
40:42.481 --> 40:44.733
‎Why didn't you tell them your name?

445
40:45.359 --> 40:46.360
‎Was it deliberate?

446
40:47.445 --> 40:48.362
‎I guess…

447
40:50.114 --> 40:52.450
‎I don't want to be remembered ‎by my name anymore.

448
41:02.585 --> 41:04.420
‎OPENING THE FUTURE ‎THROUGH ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

449
41:04.503 --> 41:06.505
‎-Mom! ‎-Gosh, Yun-jeong!

450
41:07.631 --> 41:09.508
‎-I'm sorry, sweetheart. ‎-Good job hanging in there.

451
41:09.592 --> 41:10.468
‎Ji-hye.

452
41:53.552 --> 41:54.428
‎Seon-ju.

453
42:17.618 --> 42:20.621
‎LEAVING A PROFOUND IMPACT IN HIS WAKE ‎CONDUCTOR KANG SEUNG-WOON

454
42:37.263 --> 42:38.222
‎Father.

455
42:39.181 --> 42:41.100
‎THE LATE KANG SEUNG-WOON JOHN

456
42:44.270 --> 42:45.229
‎I'm here.

457
42:55.197 --> 42:56.282
‎Hyun-soo.

458
42:58.325 --> 42:59.535
‎Thank you for today.

459
43:01.370 --> 43:04.915
‎It weighed on me not being there ‎when my father passed,

460
43:05.916 --> 43:07.543
‎but some of that weight

461
43:08.210 --> 43:09.503
‎has finally been lifted.

462
43:10.254 --> 43:11.880
‎It must have been hard for you.

463
43:12.923 --> 43:13.799
‎No.

464
43:14.341 --> 43:15.676
‎I'm much better now.

465
43:17.052 --> 43:18.679
‎You don't have to worry about me anymore.

466
43:19.263 --> 43:20.472
‎From now on,

467
43:20.556 --> 43:23.142
‎don't waste your time on me.

468
43:23.225 --> 43:24.643
‎It makes me feel bad.

469
43:25.811 --> 43:26.687
‎I can't do that.

470
43:28.647 --> 43:31.317
‎If I want to become happy…

471
43:33.193 --> 43:34.820
‎I need you by my side.

472
43:36.488 --> 43:37.865
‎I have no right to.

473
43:47.249 --> 43:49.627
‎All I need is you, Ji-hye.

474
43:50.711 --> 43:51.962
‎We'll take it easy.

475
43:56.425 --> 43:57.384
‎Like friends.

476
44:17.363 --> 44:18.530
‎Sorry.

477
44:19.365 --> 44:20.616
‎Have you been waiting long?

478
44:21.617 --> 44:23.035
‎No, I just ordered.

479
44:23.535 --> 44:25.079
‎Hurry up and eat while it's warm.

480
44:25.996 --> 44:26.955
‎It's what you wanted.

481
44:27.831 --> 44:30.209
‎I've never seen ‎a chicken sandwich this big.

482
44:30.292 --> 44:33.420
‎I'm so obsessed with it ‎that I have it for lunch every day.

483
44:39.843 --> 44:40.678
‎It's so good.

484
44:41.845 --> 44:43.597
‎Hey, go ahead and try it.

485
44:43.681 --> 44:44.598
‎Okay.

486
44:51.438 --> 44:52.314
‎This is good.

487
44:55.192 --> 44:56.110
‎Oh, right.

488
45:02.991 --> 45:03.826
‎Jae-in.

489
45:05.077 --> 45:06.286
‎It's good that you're working,

490
45:06.954 --> 45:08.497
‎but aren't you overdoing it?

491
45:09.456 --> 45:10.416
‎Don't get me started.

492
45:11.125 --> 45:12.459
‎I was just heading out the door

493
45:12.543 --> 45:15.337
‎when I heard one of our artists ‎got into trouble again.

494
45:15.421 --> 45:17.840
‎I was late because we had ‎an emergency meeting about it.

495
45:20.342 --> 45:22.136
‎I thought your trouble ended with me.

496
45:22.219 --> 45:24.680
‎I guess there's another troublemaker.

497
45:24.763 --> 45:26.932
‎Compared to the trouble you got into,

498
45:27.015 --> 45:29.017
‎this is peanuts.

499
45:29.101 --> 45:32.229
‎You're a legendary troublemaker.

500
45:39.319 --> 45:42.406
‎So, Reporter Joo Jae-geun ‎from Donggwang Daily

501
45:43.115 --> 45:45.576
‎has been begging to meet you,

502
45:45.659 --> 45:47.202
‎but I managed to put a stop to it.

503
45:48.203 --> 45:50.414
‎I'll give you his number later.

504
45:50.914 --> 45:52.332
‎If he calls, don't answer.

505
45:53.500 --> 45:54.835
‎Same goes for Reporter Han Su-jin.

506
45:54.918 --> 45:58.130
‎She asked if you were performing today,

507
45:58.797 --> 46:00.382
‎but I told her no.

508
46:01.091 --> 46:01.925
‎Okay.

509
46:02.593 --> 46:03.427
‎Thanks.

510
46:04.094 --> 46:06.388
‎Where are you performing today?

511
46:09.725 --> 46:10.726
‎Today?

512
46:21.069 --> 46:23.030
‎REGIONAL EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

513
47:02.986 --> 47:04.613
‎Excuse me. Mr. Kang?

514
47:06.406 --> 47:08.575
‎I really enjoyed your performance.

515
47:09.326 --> 47:10.994
‎I don't know much about classical music,

516
47:11.078 --> 47:13.664
‎but what you have ‎feels like a divine blessing

517
47:13.747 --> 47:15.207
‎because it strikes a chord.

518
47:15.832 --> 47:16.667
‎Thank you.

519
47:17.709 --> 47:19.169
‎By the way,

520
47:20.003 --> 47:23.131
‎do you know ‎how Conductor Choi Jeong-yo is doing?

521
47:25.050 --> 47:26.093
‎No.

522
47:26.176 --> 47:28.053
‎Oh, I see.

523
47:29.638 --> 47:33.559
‎I was just asking ‎because I was worried about his health.

524
47:35.018 --> 47:35.894
‎If you'll excuse me.

525
47:36.728 --> 47:39.022
‎Wait. What do you mean by that?

526
47:39.898 --> 47:41.525
‎Is Jeong-yo sick?

527
47:42.150 --> 47:43.277
‎Oh…

528
47:43.360 --> 47:46.405
‎I've actually been looking for Jeong-yo ‎ever since he disappeared.

529
47:47.322 --> 47:51.076
‎Please tell me whatever you know.

530
47:51.952 --> 47:54.538
‎I shouldn't have said anything.

531
47:54.621 --> 47:56.623
‎I can't share patient information.

532
47:58.417 --> 47:59.501
‎Please, sir.

533
48:00.043 --> 48:02.713
‎I really want to find Jeong-yo.

534
48:10.262 --> 48:12.055
‎Conductor Choi Jeong-yo

535
48:12.681 --> 48:15.601
‎was one of my patients who used to ‎come in for treatment regularly.

536
48:16.393 --> 48:19.062
‎A gunshot wound to the shoulder years ago

537
48:19.146 --> 48:21.898
‎left him with a brachial plexus injury,

538
48:22.399 --> 48:25.777
‎and it was causing his hand ‎to slowly lose motor function.

539
48:28.614 --> 48:31.408
‎He suddenly said ‎there was something he had to do

540
48:31.491 --> 48:33.076
‎and asked for an injection.

541
48:33.785 --> 48:36.622
‎I told him he might ‎permanently lose the use of his hand

542
48:37.205 --> 48:40.000
‎if he was overtreated like that.

543
48:40.917 --> 48:42.586
‎But I couldn't talk him out of it.

544
48:44.046 --> 48:45.756
‎So I gave him the injection.

545
48:46.590 --> 48:47.799
‎After a while,

546
48:48.550 --> 48:50.260
‎he stopped coming to see me.

547
48:50.344 --> 48:52.429
‎Then I heard he had retired,

548
48:52.512 --> 48:54.348
‎so I felt bad for him as his doctor.

549
48:54.848 --> 48:55.849
‎That's why

550
48:56.391 --> 48:59.144
‎I thought to ask you about him.

551
49:04.483 --> 49:05.692
‎Nine years ago,

552
49:06.610 --> 49:08.737
‎I got shot in my right shoulder.

553
49:09.738 --> 49:11.323
‎It caused nerve damage in my fingers.

554
49:11.406 --> 49:14.201
‎I can get through daily life, ‎but I can't play anymore.

555
49:16.828 --> 49:17.954
‎What's going on?

556
49:18.038 --> 49:20.457
‎Why? You surprised?

557
49:21.249 --> 49:24.419
‎I kept up with my hospital treatments ‎just in case.

558
49:24.503 --> 49:27.422
‎Then somehow, my fingers started working.

559
49:29.299 --> 49:30.342
‎Well?

560
49:30.425 --> 49:31.635
‎Was it any good?

561
49:47.192 --> 49:49.236
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

562
51:44.935 --> 51:47.020
‎HE'S USING HIS WRISTS DIFFERENTLY, ‎BUT I STILL THINK IT'S HIM.

563
52:00.534 --> 52:01.785
‎ANOTHER NEMESIS MASTER BESIDES KANG?

564
52:01.868 --> 52:04.204
‎I THINK IT'S KANG PI-O, PLEASE COME BACK

565
52:43.326 --> 52:45.495
‎TRY A MORE RELAXED RUBATO IN THE LEFT HAND ‎FOR THE 2ND MOVEMENT.

566
52:45.579 --> 52:47.414
‎AND STRIP OUT THE ORNAMENTS ‎IN THE MIDDLE SECTION.

567
52:52.878 --> 52:54.129
‎CZECH REPUBLIC

568
53:10.353 --> 53:12.022
‎CHURCHES IN THE CZECH REPUBLIC

569
54:07.744 --> 54:09.371
‎Why are you going there?

570
54:09.454 --> 54:11.706
‎It's not a tourist place.

571
54:11.790 --> 54:14.417
‎You can't even drive a car there.

572
54:15.335 --> 54:16.962
‎I'm here to see a friend.

573
54:17.879 --> 54:19.881
‎Oh, I see.

574
56:01.107 --> 56:02.484
‎Good job, everyone.

575
56:02.567 --> 56:06.196
‎With a little more practice, ‎we'll be good enough to perform on stage.

576
56:06.905 --> 56:10.575
‎Let's have the altos take a break ‎while the sopranos…

577
57:49.757 --> 57:51.718
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

578
57:53.219 --> 57:55.138
‎You really don't remember me?

579
57:55.221 --> 57:57.849
‎You lent me your handkerchief ‎when I asked.

580
57:58.600 --> 57:59.851
‎And we played four hands.

581
01:00:57.445 --> 01:00:58.279
‎-Play freely… ‎-Play freely…

582
01:00:59.238 --> 01:01:00.198
‎-like that day. ‎-like that day.

583
01:01:08.414 --> 01:01:13.419
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
